{"parentUuid":"f42c3333-d0d0-4098-9fa6-4dabcef7e99a","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Jv4ViCUGGDsmWJUbFwpDqt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01My1Vxvvk4fs7DwgHwpmXAo","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"OR-Tools CP-SAT shared tree search subsolver Laurent Perron"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7925,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"output_tokens":207,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7925},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":207,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7925,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7925,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot2J93hqZpgxAMLJjKX","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"e0bb84db-aeac-4563-a926-eef9f7a6834a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:34.342Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f42c3333-d0d0-4098-9fa6-4dabcef7e99a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EJsg73AbVHkbrN8V5hM5rZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT shared_tree_num_workers parameter sat_parameters.proto\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy.solvers.ortools — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/cp_optimizer/_modules/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver couldn't prove the solution is optimal if num_workers < 5 but otherwise it did instantly. · Issue #3662 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3662\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT produces nondeterministic results · Issue #3590 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3590\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy ortools interface (cpmpy.solvers.ortools) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/ufunc/api/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"Find many CP-SAT solutions, multi-threaded, under time constraint\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/GNgvcMpEwmE\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.py at master · CPMpy/cpmpy\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CPMpy/cpmpy/blob/master/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.py\"}]\n\nI found the information about the `shared_tree_num_workers` parameter in the OR-Tools CP-SAT solver. Here are the relevant details from the `sat_parameters.proto` file:\n\nThe `shared_tree_num_workers` parameter enables shared tree search. If positive, it starts that many complete worker threads to explore a shared search tree, with workers communicating objective bounds and simple decision nogoods relating to the shared prefix of the tree and avoiding exploring the same subtrees as one another.\n\nSpecifying a negative number uses a heuristic to select an appropriate number of shared tree workers based on the total number of workers.\n\nThe parameter is defined as `optional int32 shared_tree_num_workers = 235 [default = -1]`, with users not intended to set this directly.\n\nThe parameter is part of Google's OR-Tools library and is documented in the official `sat_parameters.proto` file in their GitHub repository.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0bff4851-6ba5-4d88-9363-82b5d2be5ff2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:39.717Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f42c3333-d0d0-4098-9fa6-4dabcef7e99a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e0bb84db-aeac-4563-a926-eef9f7a6834a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01My1Vxvvk4fs7DwgHwpmXAo","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT shared tree search subsolver Laurent Perron\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Custom combination of subsolvers\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/pQ4B7QD6ebw\"},{\"title\":\"Monitor search in CP-SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/r54A2eokoXk\"},{\"title\":\"Parallel search problem in CP-SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/i3TF_Szuz_k\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT claims to find optimal solution to a MILP\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/4fcAuWiIUFA\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"The CP-SAT-LP Solver Laurent Perron # Google, Paris, France Frédéric Didier #\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol280-cp2023/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Integrate GA(Genetic Algorithms) inside CP-SAT as a subsolver? · google/or-tools · Discussion #2805\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/2805\"},{\"title\":\"ViolationLS: Constraint-Based Local Search in CP-SAT | Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1007/978-3-031-60597-0_16\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant information about OR-Tools CP-SAT and Laurent Perron's work on the solver architecture.\n\nThe CP-SAT-LP solver is developed by the Operations Research team at Google and is part of the OR-Tools open-source optimization suite, with Laurent Perron at Google, Paris, France as one of the key authors.\n\nRegarding subsolvers in CP-SAT, the search results show that CP-SAT includes 11 full problem subsolvers: [core, default_lp, lb_tree_search, max_lp, no_lp, objective_lb_search, probing, pseudo_costs, quick_restart, quick_restart_no_lp, reduced_costs]. The \"lb_tree_search\" subsolver appears in this list, which may be the \"shared tree search\" subsolver you're asking about.\n\nAdditionally, search results show task timing information for various subsolvers including 'core' and 'default_lp', and clauses are shared between different subsolvers during the solving process.\n\nThe search results indicate that Laurent Perron has been actively involved in developing and documenting CP-SAT's architecture and subsolver mechanisms, though the specific details about the \"shared tree search subsolver\" implementation details would require access to the full technical documentation or research papers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0228eb36-1888-41f0-bf6f-51f0f1dcb9af","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:40.570Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e0bb84db-aeac-4563-a926-eef9f7a6834a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0228eb36-1888-41f0-bf6f-51f0f1dcb9af","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_017Y14GZHBf2jY2ab6c56anJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E9myYT6kv3QrmSq2yzQ9uZ","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto","prompt":"Find every parameter related to shared_tree, including: shared_tree_num_workers, shared_tree_worker_objective_split_probability, use_shared_tree_search, shared_tree_split_strategy, shared_tree_max_nodes_per_worker, shared_tree_open_leaves_per_worker, shared_tree_balance_tolerance. Quote the full proto field definition with field number, default value, and the comment block above each. Also list any related fields like lb_tree_search."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2634,"cache_read_input_tokens":21038,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2634,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":57,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot38uwgLhxqnTi91jdr","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"bc529e66-69d7-4f7d-abeb-5066a3710bbf","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:45.629Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
