{"parentUuid":"bc529e66-69d7-4f7d-abeb-5066a3710bbf","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E9myYT6kv3QrmSq2yzQ9uZ","type":"tool_result","content":"# Shared Tree Parameters in OR-Tools SAT\n\nBased on the provided `sat_parameters.proto` file content, **no parameters related to `shared_tree` were found**. The file excerpt does not contain any of the following fields you mentioned:\n\n- `shared_tree_num_workers`\n- `shared_tree_worker_objective_split_probability`\n- `use_shared_tree_search`\n- `shared_tree_split_strategy`\n- `shared_tree_max_nodes_per_worker`\n- `shared_tree_open_leaves_per_worker`\n- `shared_tree_balance_tolerance`\n\n## Related Field Found\n\nThe only tree-related search parameter visible in this excerpt is:\n\n**`lb_tree_search`** – mentioned in comments within the `subsolvers` field documentation as one of available solver configurations: \"lb_tree_search (to improve lower bound, MIP like tree search)\"\n\n## Note\n\nThe file shown extends to line 1000 of 1925 total lines. The shared_tree parameters may be defined in the remainder of the file not displayed in this excerpt. You would need to view the complete proto file to locate these parameters."}]},"uuid":"1d297ba8-b9c3-4295-898b-0c9566e6df88","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:49.358Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bc529e66-69d7-4f7d-abeb-5066a3710bbf","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4e959503-7a22-4a03-afdf-da2ca6d26089","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GJStsuLcoQj2Z56VgazzvQ","type":"tool_result","content":"# Search on Shared Tree Workers\n\nBased on the provided content, the CP-SAT Primer does **not mention** `shared_tree` workers, `shared_tree_num_workers`, or any distinction between shared tree mode and portfolio search.\n\nThe document exclusively discusses **portfolio mode**, which is CP-SAT's default parallelization approach. Here's what it covers:\n\n## Portfolio Search (Documented)\n\nThe primer explains that \"CP-SAT is a portfolio-solver that uses different techniques to solve the problem. There is some information exchange between the different workers, but it does not split the solution space into different parts.\"\n\nKey points about portfolio parallelization:\n\n- **Default behavior**: CP-SAT \"leverages all available cores (including hyperthreading)\" through the `num_workers` parameter\n- **Strategy**: Multiple subsolvers run simultaneously with different configurations (varying linearization, search strategies, etc.)\n- **Information sharing**: Workers exchange solutions and bounds, but don't partition the search space\n\nThe document provides a detailed table showing which subsolvers activate at different worker counts (1, 2, 3, 4... up to 64+), but makes no reference to alternative search modes like shared tree parallelization.\n\n**Conclusion**: The primer addresses portfolio search exclusively and contains no information about shared tree workers or how they differ from portfolio mode."}]},"uuid":"c46324df-8c34-4741-80f4-900dfaa4e8e6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:51.980Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4e959503-7a22-4a03-afdf-da2ca6d26089","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
