{"parentUuid":"11c93644-830b-4809-84c1-a7429b860836","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_017dqGHe5UZ9T7Ps7tDLec4g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UhMMSXBv5hpYePQTboDV1b","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"OR-Tools CP-SAT shared_tree github issue parallel search nogood"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1342,"cache_read_input_tokens":23672,"output_tokens":361,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1342},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":361,"cache_read_input_tokens":23672,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1342,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1342,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot3yqGpTcJtjaNJPDKM","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ce34f4c4-9a78-4194-bfb8-0b314312d192","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:58.767Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"11c93644-830b-4809-84c1-a7429b860836","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ab8o5DcLoANyzF1eBGTTB4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"shared_tree_worker_objective_split_probability\" OR \"shared_tree_split_strategy\" OR-Tools\"\n\nNo links found.\n\nThe search returned no results for that specific query. This suggests that these parameter names or configuration options may be:\n\n1. Very specialized/niche technical parameters that aren't well-indexed by search engines\n2. Internal implementation details that aren't widely documented online\n3. Parameters from a specific version or branch of OR-Tools that isn't commonly discussed\n4. Potentially misspelled or from a non-standard naming convention\n\nIf you're looking for information about OR-Tools tree-based algorithms or decision tree splitting strategies, I'd be happy to search for more general terms. Alternatively, if you have more context about what you're trying to accomplish with these parameters, I can help you find relevant documentation or implementation details.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c61ecd0a-5574-4d0d-a175-dd747a35e818","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:02.632Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"11c93644-830b-4809-84c1-a7429b860836","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ce34f4c4-9a78-4194-bfb8-0b314312d192","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UhMMSXBv5hpYePQTboDV1b","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT shared_tree github issue parallel search nogood\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT produces nondeterministic results · Issue #3590 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3590\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"Parallel solving returns unknown status · google/or-tools · Discussion #2873\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/2873\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Find many CP-SAT solutions, multi-threaded, under time constraint\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/GNgvcMpEwmE\"},{\"title\":\"CP-Sat: Python 3.7.2, ortools 7.0 wrong optimization result · Issue #1162 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1162\"},{\"title\":\"Multithreading: solving different problems with CP-SAT ends in random crash · Issue #1958 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1958\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver couldn't prove the solution is optimal if num_workers < 5 but otherwise it did instantly. · Issue #3662 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3662\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint solver beginner questions: can it be multi-threaded? How can I improve speed? · Issue #933 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/933\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: not all threads are used, why? · Issue #2399 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/2399\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about OR-Tools CP-SAT's shared tree search feature with parallel workers. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Shared Tree Search Parameters\n\nWorkers in shared tree search communicate objective bounds and simple decision nogoods relating to the shared prefix of the tree, and will avoid exploring the same subtrees as one another. The configuration is controlled through the `shared_tree_num_workers` parameter with a default value of -1.\n\nSpecifying a negative number uses a heuristic to select an appropriate number of shared tree workers based on the total number of workers.\n\n## GitHub Issues Related to Parallel Search\n\nThere are several GitHub issues discussing problems with parallel search in CP-SAT:\n\n1. **Issue #3590**: With versions 9.4 and 9.5, the solver produces nondeterministic solutions when disabling parallelism with num_search_workers set to 1.\n\n2. **Issue #3662**: Discusses a case where CP-SAT couldn't prove optimal solutions when num_workers < 5 but could with more workers.\n\n3. **Solution Enumeration Limitation**: Enumerating all solutions in parallel is not supported in CP-SAT.\n\nThe search results show that the shared tree search uses nogoods to coordinate work between parallel workers and prevent redundant exploration of the solution space.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"833b7f7e-9af3-435b-95ef-01b1d9f15e4e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:05.613Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ce34f4c4-9a78-4194-bfb8-0b314312d192","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"5e7baf96-00fa-4da3-85c2-bafd76d93d82","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015pZNfSRriQX2q2uMYTYTW9","type":"tool_result","content":"# Fields Containing \"shared_tree\" or \"lb_tree_search\"\n\n## shared_tree_num_workers\n```\n  // Enables shared tree search.\n  // If positive, start this many complete worker threads to explore a shared\n  // search tree. These workers communicate objective bounds and simple decision\n  // nogoods relating to the shared prefix of the tree, and will avoid exploring\n  // the same subtrees as one another.\n  // Specifying a negative number uses a heuristic to select an appropriate\n  // number of shared tree workeres based on the total number of workers.\n  optional int32 shared_tree_num_workers = 235 [default = -1];\n```\n\n## use_shared_tree_search\n```\n  // Set on shared subtree workers. Users should not set this directly.\n  optional bool use_shared_tree_search = 236 [default = false];\n```\n\n## shared_tree_worker_min_restarts_per_subtree\n```\n  // Minimum restarts before a worker will replace a subtree\n  // that looks \"bad\" based on the average LBD of learned clauses.\n  optional int32 shared_tree_worker_min_restarts_per_subtree = 282\n      [default = 1];\n```\n\n## shared_tree_worker_enable_trail_sharing\n```\n  // If true, workers share more of the information from their local trail.\n  // Specifically, literals implied by the shared tree decisions.\n  optional bool shared_tree_worker_enable_trail_sharing = 295 [default = true];\n```\n\n## shared_tree_worker_enable_phase_sharing\n```\n  // If true, shared tree workers share their target phase when returning an\n  // assigned subtree for the next worker to use.\n  optional bool shared_tree_worker_enable_phase_sharing = 304 [default = true];\n```\n\n## shared_tree_open_leaves_per_worker\n```\n  // How many open leaf nodes should the shared tree maintain per worker.\n  optional double shared_tree_open_leaves_per_worker = 281 [default = 2.0];\n```\n\n## shared_tree_max_nodes_per_worker\n```\n  // In order to limit total shared memory and communication overhead, limit the\n  // total number of nodes that may be generated in the shared tree. If the\n  // shared tree runs out of unassigned leaves, workers act as portfolio\n  // workers. Note: this limit includes interior nodes, not just leaves.\n  optional int32 shared_tree_max_nodes_per_worker = 238 [default = 10000];\n```\n\n## shared_tree_split_strategy\n```\n  enum SharedTreeSplitStrategy {\n    // Uses the default strategy, currently equivalent to\n    // SPLIT_STRATEGY_DISCREPANCY.\n    SPLIT_STRATEGY_AUTO = 0;\n    // Only accept splits if the node to be split's depth+discrepancy is minimal\n    // for the desired number of leaves.\n    // The preferred child for discrepancy calculation is the one with the\n    // lowest objective lower bound or the original branch direction if the\n    // bounds are equal. This rule allows twice as many workers to work in the\n    // preferred subtree as non-preferred.\n    SPLIT_STRATEGY_DISCREPANCY = 1;\n    // Only split nodes with an objective lb equal to the global lb. If there is\n    // no objective, this is equivalent to SPLIT_STRATEGY_FIRST_PROPOSAL.\n    SPLIT_STRATEGY_OBJECTIVE_LB = 2;\n    // Attempt to keep the shared tree balanced.\n    SPLIT_STRATEGY_BALANCED_TREE = 3;\n    // Workers race to split their subtree, the winner's proposal is accepted.\n    SPLIT_STRATEGY_FIRST_PROPOSAL = 4;\n  }\n  optional SharedTreeSplitStrategy shared_tree_split_strategy = 239\n      [default = SPLIT_STRATEGY_AUTO];\n```\n\n## shared_tree_balance_tolerance\n```\n  // How much deeper compared to the ideal max depth of the tree is considered\n  // \"balanced\" enough to still accept a split. Without such a tolerance,\n  // sometimes the tree can only be split by a single worker, and they may not\n  // generate a split for some time. In contrast, with a tolerance of 1, at\n  // least half of all workers should be able to split the tree as soon as a\n  // split becomes required. This only has an effect on\n  // SPLIT_STRATEGY_BALANCED_TREE and SPLIT_STRATEGY_DISCREPANCY.\n  optional int32 shared_tree_balance_tolerance = 305 [default = 1];\n```\n\n## shared_tree_split_min_dtime\n```\n  // How much dtime a worker will wait between proposing splits.\n  // This limits the contention in splitting the shared tree, and also reduces\n  // the number of too-easy subtrees that are generates.\n  optional double shared_tree_split_min_dtime = 328 [default = 0.1];\n```\n\n## optimize_with_lb_tree_search\n```\n  // Do a more conventional tree search (by opposition to SAT based one) where\n  // we keep all the explored node in a tree. This is meant to be used in a\n  // portfolio and focus on improving the objective lower bound. Keeping the\n  // whole tree allow us to report a better objective lower bound coming from\n  // the worst open node in the tree.\n  optional bool optimize_with_lb_tree_search = 188 [default = false];\n```\n\n## save_lp_basis_in_lb_tree_search\n```\n  // Experimental. Save the current LP basis at each node of the search tree so\n  // that when we jump around, we can load it and reduce the number of LP\n  // iterations needed.\n  //\n  // It currently works okay if we do not change the lp with cuts or\n  // simplification... More work is needed to make it robust in all cases.\n  optional bool save_lp_basis_in_lb_tree_search = 284 [default = false];\n```"}]},"uuid":"c65dceee-8137-42aa-ac39-03014e99764c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:14.197Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5e7baf96-00fa-4da3-85c2-bafd76d93d82","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
