{"parentUuid":"e5b2bd44-fa1f-45eb-9254-6ea7b6d17e66","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01QY1Lxv4gdbxeUyqfmHsxzR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BvXwMZ3Svvo2XArHiNCGk4","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"OR-Tools shared_tree_num_workers heuristic default subsolvers list parallel"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1594,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2385,"cache_read_input_tokens":25014,"output_tokens":485,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2385},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1594,"output_tokens":485,"cache_read_input_tokens":25014,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2385,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2385,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot5cuz96KUvqfqk8zof","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"7aa239c0-4a14-46ba-8eb5-fa38ffeda9d0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:21.522Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3230cd42-fe98-4910-a057-aa6a21915472","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MNyeTRsHbiUD3JnmSGuTRy","type":"tool_result","content":"Based on the provided code, I cannot find any functions or logic related to `SetupSharedTreeManager`, `NumSharedTreeWorkers`, or specific handling of `shared_tree_num_workers` when negative.\n\nThe only reference to shared_tree in this file appears in the `GetNamedParameters` function:\n\n```cpp\n{\n    SatParameters new_params = base_params;\n    new_params.set_use_shared_tree_search(true);\n    new_params.set_search_branching(SatParameters::AUTOMATIC_SEARCH);\n    \n    new_params.set_optimize_with_core(false);\n    new_params.set_optimize_with_lb_tree_search(false);\n    new_params.set_optimize_with_max_hs(false);\n    \n    new_params.set_polarity_exploit_ls_hints(false);\n    \n    strategies[\"shared_tree\"] = new_params;\n}\n```\n\nThis code simply creates a named strategy configuration for shared_tree, but does not contain logic for activating shared_tree workers, handling negative worker counts, or managing the shared tree setup. The activation logic you're looking for appears to be in a different source file not provided here."}]},"uuid":"a4cc6cba-bf76-4eae-8154-4dd2a6332f04","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:23.172Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3230cd42-fe98-4910-a057-aa6a21915472","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e5b2bd44-fa1f-45eb-9254-6ea7b6d17e66","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SiCKSpU5QTNVwsQgaCmwfc","type":"tool_result","content":"# Shared Tree Workers in work_assignment.h\n\n## Class Definition\n\nThe file contains the `SharedTreeWorker` class, which implements a parallel search strategy. The constructor is:\n\n```cpp\nexplicit SharedTreeWorker(Model* model);\n```\n\n## Algorithm Description\n\nThe core algorithm is explained in this comment:\n\n> \"Scalable Parallelization of Learning Solvers\" (Graeme Gange & Peter Stuckey's proposal)\n\nThe implementation uses a **tree splitting and work distribution approach**:\n\n> \"The core idea of this implementation is that workers can maintain several ProtoTrails, and periodically replace the 'worst' one. With 1 assignment per worker, this leads to something very similar to Embarassingly Parallel Search.\"\n\nWorkers explore subtrees assigned by a `SharedTreeManager`, which supports:\n- `TrySplitTree()`: Repeatedly branches the search tree with accepted splits\n- `ReplaceTree()`: Assigns new path prefixes to explore\n- `CloseTree()`: Marks explored subtrees as containing no improving solutions\n\n## Synchronization Primitives\n\nThe code uses:\n\n- **`absl::Mutex`** (`mu_`): Guards the shared tree state with `ABSL_LOCKS_EXCLUDED` and `ABSL_EXCLUSIVE_LOCKS_REQUIRED` annotations\n- **Thread-safe response management** via `SharedResponseManager`\n- **LRAT proof handling** for concurrent clause verification\n\nThe worker synchronizes with both the local solver trail and the shared tree through `SyncWithLocalTrail()` and `SyncWithSharedTree()` methods."}]},"uuid":"48144998-6666-4275-88cd-d9e9364bf112","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:27.814Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e5b2bd44-fa1f-45eb-9254-6ea7b6d17e66","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7aa239c0-4a14-46ba-8eb5-fa38ffeda9d0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BvXwMZ3Svvo2XArHiNCGk4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools shared_tree_num_workers heuristic default subsolvers list parallel\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Infeasibility Subsolvers\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/Tz8ovW6cZtY\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Custom combination of subsolvers\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/pQ4B7QD6ebw\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver couldn't prove the solution is optimal if num_workers < 5 but otherwise it did instantly. · Issue #3662 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3662\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"Segmentation fault running CP-SAT with 1 worker using free-search in 9.11 · Issue #4412 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4412\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools: ortools/sat/docs/troubleshooting.md | Fossies\",\"url\":\"https://fossies.org/linux/or-tools/ortools/sat/docs/troubleshooting.md\"},{\"title\":\"Get nondeterministic results with different number of workers using CP-SAT; Optimal using 1 worker, Infeasible using 8 workers · Issue #3842 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3842\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT produces nondeterministic results · Issue #3590 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3590\"},{\"title\":\"Force CP-SAT to use some specific subsolvers.\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/_UOHuLu7Nws\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Release Notes | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/support/release_notes\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding OR-Tools CP-SAT subsolvers and parallel search configuration:\n\n## Default Subsolvers List\n\nWith 8 workers, OR-Tools CP-SAT uses the minimum number of workers needed to trigger parallel search, blending workers with different linear relaxations (none, default, maximal), core-based search if applicable, a quick_restart subsolver, a feasibility_jump first solution subsolver, and dedicated Large Neighborhood Search subsolvers.\n\nWith 16 workers, the configuration adds a continuous probing subsolver, more first solution subsolvers (random search and feasibility_jump), two dual subsolvers dedicated to improving the lower bound of the objective (when minimizing), and more LNS subsolvers.\n\n## Subsolver Categories\n\nA typical 16-worker configuration includes 11 full problem subsolvers: [core, default_lp, lb_tree_search, max_lp, no_lp, objective_lb_search, probing, pseudo_costs, quick_restart, quick_restart_no_lp, reduced_costs], 4 first solution subsolvers, and 12 incomplete subsolvers.\n\n## Worker Control\n\nRegarding `shared_tree_num_workers`, the search results don't contain specific documentation about this parameter, but they indicate that the solver is tuned for 8 and 16 workers.\n\nFor more specific information about the `shared_tree_num_workers` parameter and detailed heuristic configuration, you may need to consult the official OR-Tools documentation or source code directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5b7bb447-4a65-46b5-95d8-0469e14cb482","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:28.748Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7aa239c0-4a14-46ba-8eb5-fa38ffeda9d0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"5b7bb447-4a65-46b5-95d8-0469e14cb482","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01TRDbZuNXgGzTWatr4jesjC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PHKd1zQugWfRX7sTnWiwB5","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/or-tools/stable/ortools/sat/cp_model_solver_helpers.cc","prompt":"Find any code related to shared_tree_num_workers, shared tree subsolver activation, or the heuristic that picks shared tree worker count when shared_tree_num_workers is -1. Also find the function that builds the subsolver list and any references to \"shared_tree\" name. Quote code verbatim."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4413,"cache_read_input_tokens":27399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4413,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot6gpfDfa3cbmk4rkxR","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"98197148-9480-4697-8145-4917e3fb0cfd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:33.022Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"98197148-9480-4697-8145-4917e3fb0cfd","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01TRDbZuNXgGzTWatr4jesjC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LLsyHLQrt5iHz4gRYt7SJL","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/or-tools/stable/ortools/sat/work_assignment.cc","prompt":"Quote the comments and constructor of SharedTreeManager and SharedTreeWorker. What's the algorithm in plain English? How does TrySplitTree work? How does the heuristic for default num workers work? Also look for any references to \"Gange\" or \"Stuckey\" or papers, and any default values for parameters."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4413,"cache_read_input_tokens":27399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4413,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot6gpfDfa3cbmk4rkxR","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"482b1362-3acc-4675-a109-e49adc95248d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:35.704Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"482b1362-3acc-4675-a109-e49adc95248d","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01TRDbZuNXgGzTWatr4jesjC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VWeYgoDcJYzCL1BnUBhKti","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3662","prompt":"What does this issue say about the role of shared_tree workers, num_workers thresholds for activating subsolvers, and Laurent Perron's explanations? Quote relevant comments."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4413,"cache_read_input_tokens":27399,"output_tokens":574,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4413},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":574,"cache_read_input_tokens":27399,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4413,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4413,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot6gpfDfa3cbmk4rkxR","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"62935671-f28f-4f69-a9f6-9a82e9cb8328","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:36.742Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"98197148-9480-4697-8145-4917e3fb0cfd","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PHKd1zQugWfRX7sTnWiwB5","type":"tool_result","content":"# Shared Tree Worker Configuration\n\n## Initial Setup\nThe code initializes `shared_tree_num_workers` with this heuristic:\n\n```\nif (params->shared_tree_num_workers() == -1) {\n  int num_shared_tree_workers = 0;\n  if (model_proto.has_objective() ||\n      model_proto.has_floating_point_objective()) {\n    num_shared_tree_workers = (params->num_workers() - 16) / 2;\n  } else {\n    num_shared_tree_workers = (params->num_workers() - 8) * 3 / 4;\n  }\n```\n\nThis logic allocates shared tree workers based on total workers and problem type—optimization problems receive fewer shared tree workers than decision problems.\n\n## Usage References\n\nThe subsolver activates via parameter checks:\n\n```\nif (parameters.use_shared_tree_search()) {\n  auto* subtree_worker = model->GetOrCreate<SharedTreeWorker>();\n  status = subtree_worker->Search(solution_observer);\n}\n```\n\nThe `SharedTreeManager` class gets registered in shared classes when needed, allowing local models to access the shared tree infrastructure through `model->GetOrCreate<SharedTreeManager>()`."}]},"uuid":"be51ec20-3774-4ffb-aaa6-b87221f4b19f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:37.539Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"98197148-9480-4697-8145-4917e3fb0cfd","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"62935671-f28f-4f69-a9f6-9a82e9cb8328","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VWeYgoDcJYzCL1BnUBhKti","type":"tool_result","content":"I cannot find any comments from Laurent Perron or discussions about shared_tree workers and num_workers thresholds in the provided webpage content. \n\nThe page shows only the **initial issue report** by lucidfrontier45, which describes:\n\n- A CP-SAT solver behavior discrepancy where `num_workers=4` failed to prove optimality (60 seconds, feasible only) while `num_workers=5` proved it instantly\n- The issue was assigned to @lperron but no actual comments or explanations from him appear in this excerpt\n\nTo find Perron's analysis or technical explanations about worker thresholds and subsolver activation, you would need to access the comments section of the issue, which is not included in the content provided."}]},"uuid":"f95f61e5-7ff8-4d87-bb67-a89f3b99c8ae","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:39.610Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"62935671-f28f-4f69-a9f6-9a82e9cb8328","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"482b1362-3acc-4675-a109-e49adc95248d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LLsyHLQrt5iHz4gRYt7SJL","type":"tool_result","content":"# SharedTreeManager and SharedTreeWorker Analysis\n\n## Comments and Constructors\n\n**SharedTreeManager Constructor:**\n```cpp\nSharedTreeManager::SharedTreeManager(Model* model)\n    : params_(*model->GetOrCreate<SatParameters>()),\n      num_workers_(std::max(0, params_.shared_tree_num_workers())),\n      max_path_depth_(MaxPossibleLeafDepth(params_)),\n```\nCreates root node with fake decision, initializes unassigned leaves.\n\n**SharedTreeWorker Constructor:**\nNo explicit comments provided in the source, but it initializes numerous references to model components (SAT solver, trail, encoder, etc.) and an assigned tree with LBD window tracking.\n\n## Algorithm in Plain English\n\nThe shared tree algorithm coordinates multiple SAT solver workers exploring a single decision tree:\n\n1. **Tree Management**: A central manager maintains a shared search tree with nodes representing decision points. Workers explore different branches (leaves) of this tree.\n\n2. **Synchronization**: When workers sync, they update the tree with objective lower bounds and learned implications, potentially closing branches proven infeasible.\n\n3. **Splitting**: As workers complete subtrees, the manager splits promising leaves into new branches, maintaining balanced tree exploration across workers.\n\n4. **Trail Sharing**: Workers can share implications discovered during propagation, allowing others to benefit from learning.\n\n## How TrySplitTree Works\n\nThe method attempts to split the current leaf node along a decision sequence:\n\n1. Validates the path hasn't been invalidated by restart\n2. Checks if current node is unsplit and not closed\n3. Verifies sufficient capacity (< max_nodes_)\n4. Confirms splits are still wanted\n5. Applies split strategy heuristic (discrepancy-based or balanced tree)\n6. Creates two children nodes (positive/negative literal branches)\n7. Adds one child to explored path, queues sibling for future assignment\n\n## Default Number of Workers\n\nThe code doesn't specify a default worker count—it reads from `params_.shared_tree_num_workers()` with `std::max(0, ...)` guard. The SatParameters protobuf likely contains the actual default.\n\n## Paper References\n\nThe code contains no explicit citations to \"Gange,\" \"Stuckey,\" or academic papers in comments.\n\n## Default Parameter Values Found\n\n- `kNumInitialRestarts = 10`: Number of restarts before ending initial restart phase\n- `shared_tree_open_leaves_per_worker()`: Used to calculate splits_wanted\n- `shared_tree_balance_tolerance()`: Added to max depth calculation\n- `shared_tree_worker_min_restarts_per_subtree()`: Threshold before replacing subtree"}]},"uuid":"9a881711-21b3-4472-bb88-b9ce94962ff6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:44.688Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"482b1362-3acc-4675-a109-e49adc95248d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
