{"parentUuid":"56b85702-3c10-4d0b-a07d-4e2331fe3550","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01UpzMGdbw1JQQi6wjFE63DQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XL54HqqVr2bmRQxXVUh6wL","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html","prompt":"What does this primer say about shared_tree workers in the log? How do you identify shared tree subsolver contributions in the CP-SAT log output? Look for \"shared_tree\", subsolver tables, and any explanation of multiple parallel worker types."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":261,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1983,"cache_read_input_tokens":31812,"output_tokens":345,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1983},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":261,"output_tokens":345,"cache_read_input_tokens":31812,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1983,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1983,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot7sBnEi8o5SzAhsv8a","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"cd039a9c-102a-4f03-8188-e67dae933298","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:50.948Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c6929893-ec66-4922-8ba3-a99b7445a4e9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LQTQvqjocGPhM1wx97ercB","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Scalable Parallelization of Learning Solvers\" Gange Stuckey CP-SAT\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parallelizing Constraint Programming with Learning\",\"url\":\"https://people.eng.unimelb.edu.au/pstuckey/papers/parallelCP.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Parallelising Lazy Clause Generation with Trail Sharing | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-95973-8_13\"},{\"title\":\"Massively Parallel Continuous Local Search for Hybrid SAT Solving on GPUs\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/view/33211/35366\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Scalable Parallel Numerical CSP Solver | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-10428-7_30\"},{\"title\":\"Lazy Clause Generation: Combining the Power of SAT and CP (and MIP?) Solving | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-13520-0_3\"},{\"title\":\"Designing Scalable Parallel SAT Solvers | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-31612-8_17\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"An overview of parallel SAT solving | Constraints | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10601-012-9121-3\"},{\"title\":\"Parallelization of SAT Algorithms on GPU\",\"url\":\"https://fenix.tecnico.ulisboa.pt/downloadFile/395146459368/thesis.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found highly relevant information about this research topic:\n\n## Search Results\n\nThe research investigates the effectiveness of splitting the search space in parallelising the state-of-the-art CP-SAT solver. One of the key barriers to effective search-space splitting in learning solvers is that the generated sub-problems are not independent, leading to substantial communication-related overhead, substantial redundant work, or both.\n\nThe work's contributions attempt to mitigate this issue through job reassignment and trail sharing, where jobs (sub-trees) are reassigned to new workers if the clause database of the currently assigned worker appears ill-suited to the region of the search-space, and workers can share some of the state from their local trail.\n\nThe research appears to be authored by Gange and Stuckey (among others) and addresses the practical challenges of parallelizing constraint programming solvers with learning capabilities like CP-SAT, focusing on methods to improve efficiency when distributing work across multiple processors.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3c705f9b-fcea-4fd0-a716-2b06290d5727","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:53.415Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c6929893-ec66-4922-8ba3-a99b7445a4e9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"56b85702-3c10-4d0b-a07d-4e2331fe3550","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KHhekoFzrqkCntsv2PGHCM","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools 9.11 9.12 release notes shared_tree improvements changelog\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"v9.12 · google/or-tools · Discussion #4544\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/4544\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/releases\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Release Notes | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/support/release_notes\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools - Google Optimization Tools - Browse /v9.12 at SourceForge.net\",\"url\":\"https://sourceforge.net/projects/or-tools.mirror/files/v9.12/\"},{\"title\":\"google/or-tools v9.12 on GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://newreleases.io/project/github/google/or-tools/release/v9.12\"},{\"title\":\"Release v9.12 (2025/02) · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/releases/tag/v9.12\"},{\"title\":\"Release v9.13 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/releases/tag/v9.13\"},{\"title\":\"NuGet Gallery | Google.OrTools.runtime.osx-x64 9.12.4544\",\"url\":\"https://www.nuget.org/packages/Google.OrTools.runtime.osx-x64/9.12.4544\"},{\"title\":\"ortools Version: 9.12.4544 not working with gurobi Version: 12.0.1 · Issue #4625 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4625\"},{\"title\":\"open-vm-tools/ReleaseNotes.md at master · vmware/open-vm-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/vmware/open-vm-tools/blob/master/ReleaseNotes.md\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding OR-Tools 9.11 and 9.12 release notes with shared_tree improvements:\n\n## OR-Tools v9.12 Release (February 2025)\n\nThe v9.12 release includes improvements to shared tree workers and implementation of job affinity with workers. This was a significant enhancement compared to the previous version.\n\n### Performance Improvements\n\nA known large problem that took about 85 seconds with 9.11 now takes about 56 seconds with 9.12 to converge to optimal on a laptop with 8 workers (8 threads CPU), demonstrating the effectiveness of the shared tree worker improvements.\n\n### Additional v9.12 Features\n\nBeyond the shared tree improvements, the release also includes Xpress support, speedup of the Python expression part, and HiGHS support.\n\n### Platform Updates\n\nv9.12 will be the last release to support Python 3.8, adds Python 3.13 support, and adds a muslinux wheel package.\n\nFor the complete changelog between versions, the search results reference a full changelog available at the GitHub repository comparing v9.11 to v9.12.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"14eed8fc-d2db-491b-b5a3-05d9341d8fb1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:54.810Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"56b85702-3c10-4d0b-a07d-4e2331fe3550","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cd039a9c-102a-4f03-8188-e67dae933298","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XL54HqqVr2bmRQxXVUh6wL","type":"tool_result","content":"# Shared Tree Workers in CP-SAT Logs\n\nBased on the provided primer content, **there is no mention of \"shared_tree\" workers or shared tree subsolver contributions** in the log output documentation.\n\nThe primer discusses various subsolver types that appear in logs, including:\n- Full problem subsolvers (like `lb_tree_search`)\n- First solution subsolvers\n- Incomplete subsolvers\n- Helper subsolvers\n\nHowever, the document does not explain how to identify shared tree worker contributions or provide any specific guidance on interpreting shared tree subsolver activity in the log output.\n\nThe subsolver details section notes that it covers \"how the various subsolvers have been contributing to the solution,\" but the actual explanation focuses on LP-techniques and heuristics rather than addressing shared tree workers specifically.\n\n**To find information about shared tree workers, you would need to consult additional CP-SAT documentation beyond this primer.**"}]},"uuid":"f508ec93-b83a-4b23-8d0f-8fee3ef9f868","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:54.833Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cd039a9c-102a-4f03-8188-e67dae933298","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
