{"parentUuid":"7b00149a-4a81-4468-8c9b-10c292df1a1b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c7a9c836-fcfa-483d-8466-444dc60bbf86","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Badgu3eCHkjMqFsbNqYRCX","type":"tool_result","content":"# Summary: Shared Tree Search in Constraint Programming\n\n## The Algorithm\n\nThe paper presents a **shared tree search** approach where multiple parallel solvers work on a single, unified search tree rather than independent trees. Workers explore different branches simultaneously, sharing learned constraints (cuts and nogoods) to accelerate the overall search.\n\n## Key Differences from Portfolio Search\n\nPortfolio search runs independent solvers on identical problems in parallel. Shared tree search fundamentally differs by:\n\n- Maintaining one collaborative tree structure instead of separate instances\n- Dynamically distributing unexplored nodes among workers\n- Propagating learned constraints across all workers in real-time\n\n## Problem Classes That Benefit Most\n\nThe approach excels on:\n- **Hard combinatorial problems** with substantial symmetry or structure\n- **Mixed-integer programming** instances where cuts prove valuable across branches\n- Problems where \"early good pruning decisions help all workers\"\n\n## Infeasibility vs. Optimality Proving\n\nThe paper distinguishes two modes:\n\n> \"in shared tree mode, workers can prove infeasibility of the current subproblem independently but must cooperate to prove optimality\" \n\nThis means proving no solution exists is cheaper than proving the best solution found is optimal—requiring global coordination for the latter but not the former.\n\n## Specific Results\n\nThe paper reports shared tree search achieves **speedups of 5-10x on select benchmarks** compared to sequential solving, though gains vary significantly by problem structure and instance difficulty.\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 698.6KB) also saved to C:\\Users\\22957\\.claude\\projects\\D--claude-pj-zmd\\7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\\tool-results\\webfetch-1778187666119-7h8pfb.pdf]"}]},"uuid":"18161d21-f56b-40fb-836a-8d775e0747d5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:01:11.963Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7b00149a-4a81-4468-8c9b-10c292df1a1b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
