{"parentUuid":"ef563fd1-acc1-4a0c-894e-4606d9ff3055","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01QVSwDfvWcUPDM3XTzkGs9n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017uSY2a3j3t9CkEtWQLhPPV","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/i3TF_Szuz_k","prompt":"What does this discussion say about shared_tree workers, parallel search, when shared_tree is good or bad? Quote any responses from Laurent Perron."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":180,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1161,"cache_read_input_tokens":36945,"output_tokens":492,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1161},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":180,"output_tokens":492,"cache_read_input_tokens":36945,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1161,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1161,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot9stWKSqMQ6d1V3jTN","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"321f24d0-1d6c-4f7e-9d93-afef14c21089","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:01:20.441Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"321f24d0-1d6c-4f7e-9d93-afef14c21089","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c7a9c836-fcfa-483d-8466-444dc60bbf86","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017uSY2a3j3t9CkEtWQLhPPV","type":"tool_result","content":"# Discussion Analysis: Shared Tree Workers and Parallel Search\n\nThe provided discussion does not mention \"shared_tree workers\" at all. \n\nRegarding parallel search, Laurent Perron addresses the original question about multi-threading performance:\n\n**Key Quote from Laurent Perron:**\n\"Currently, parallel search is not deterministic. We will make it deterministic in the future, but it will degrade performance.\"\n\nHe also notes: \"For best performance, I would use 8 threads. To have speedup, you do need 8 cores, otherwise other threads will slow down the lucky one that will find a good solution.\"\n\n**Summary:** The discussion focuses on why parallel search showed inconsistent performance (varying between 16-21 seconds across runs) rather than the expected speedup. Laurent explains this variability stems from the non-deterministic nature of parallel search. He recommends 8 threads and sufficient CPU cores for meaningful speedup. The conversation later shifts toward improving the model formulation and search heuristics rather than further exploring parallelization strategies."}]},"uuid":"3ca87f18-6bf4-4ec6-bb5e-d8dc35a6cd64","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:01:24.630Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"321f24d0-1d6c-4f7e-9d93-afef14c21089","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"99adf497-7943-4ffa-af94-0bfc0dc40548","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c7a9c836-fcfa-483d-8466-444dc60bbf86","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JJ5Pn2kR5SdJ28v43Z5FH5","type":"tool_result","content":"I appreciate your question, but I need to be direct: the content you've provided appears to be a PDF file rendered as compressed binary data, not readable text. The document contains encoded streams and objects typical of PDF format, which I cannot meaningfully parse or search for specific terms like \"shared_tree,\" \"parallel architecture,\" or references to worker counts.\n\nTo properly answer your question about the CP-SAT-LP solver paper by Perron and Didier (2023), I would need:\n\n1. **Readable text content** - Either the PDF converted to plain text, or the paper provided in an accessible format\n2. **Clear source material** - Direct access to the actual document content\n\nFrom the binary data shown, I cannot reliably identify:\n- Whether this is actually the CP-SAT-LP paper you're asking about\n- Specific discussions of shared tree search mechanisms\n- Details about parallel architecture or portfolio approaches\n- Worker count specifications\n\n**I recommend:**\n- Providing the paper as plain text or properly extracted PDF content\n- Linking to the paper's location if it's publicly available\n- Sharing relevant excerpts directly\n\nOnce you provide readable content, I'll be happy to locate and quote relevant sections about parallel solver architecture within your 125-character quote limit.\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 323.5KB) also saved to C:\\Users\\22957\\.claude\\projects\\D--claude-pj-zmd\\7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\\tool-results\\webfetch-1778187680495-3cyxyx.pdf]"}]},"uuid":"fc624a8a-8779-4b91-9e88-6a75e2be11d8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:01:25.376Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"99adf497-7943-4ffa-af94-0bfc0dc40548","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","