{"parentUuid":"e130f414-7f5d-4c6e-a0a1-14a65b520353","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"2ff5202a-4e67-4036-a6e3-b87208b2fc72","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018g5evkC4VhsTaF5VFMHGev","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT log \"shared_tree\" subsolver name parallel worker portfolio\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Custom combination of subsolvers\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/pQ4B7QD6ebw\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-logutils: Utils for parsing the logs of OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-logutils\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver couldn't prove the solution is optimal if num_workers < 5 but otherwise it did instantly. · Issue #3662 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3662\"},{\"title\":\"cpsat-logutils · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/cpsat-logutils/\"},{\"title\":\"Community Branching for Parallel Portfolio SAT Solvers | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-09284-3_14\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found comprehensive information about CP-SAT logs and the parallel worker portfolio architecture, though the specific term \"shared_tree\" subsolver wasn't explicitly mentioned in these results.\n\n## Key Findings:\n\nCP-SAT is a portfolio-solver that uses different techniques to solve the problem. The solver starts search with multiple workers and uses various categories of subsolvers including full problem subsolvers, first solution subsolvers, incomplete subsolvers, and helper subsolvers.\n\nRegarding the parallel worker portfolio architecture:\n\n- With a single worker, only the default subsolver is used, while with two workers or more, CP-SAT starts using incomplete subsolvers such as LNS (Large Neighborhood Search).\n\n- There is some information exchange between the different workers, but it does not split the solution space into different parts, thus, it does not parallelize the branch-and-bound algorithm as MIP-solvers do.\n\n- These elements operate largely independently but engage in information exchange, sharing progress when better solutions emerge or tighter bounds become available.\n\nThe search results contain examples of various subsolvers including core, default_lp, lb_tree_search, max_lp, no_lp, and various LNS variants, but the specific \"shared_tree\" subsolver name you mentioned doesn't appear in the available documentation. It's possible this is a less commonly documented subsolver or a specialized variant for certain problem types.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"512ca98d-05ed-410c-84eb-77ca46b250ec","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:01:39.405Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e130f414-7f5d-4c6e-a0a1-14a65b520353","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"966ba0b1-67fb-4b27-b18f-d5489c9d4d0e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"2ff5202a-4e67-4036-a6e3-b87208b2fc72","agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AiUdKbpsXKgWdHQdup8HG3","type":"tool_result","content":"# File Header and Class Comments\n\n**Top-of-file comment:** The file is licensed under Apache License 2.0 (2010-2025 Google LLC).\n\n**SharedTreeManager class comment:**\n\"Experimental thread-safe class for managing work assignments between workers. This API is intended to investigate Graeme Gange & Peter Stuckey's proposal 'Scalable Parallelization of Learning Solvers'.\" The core approach involves workers maintaining multiple ProtoTrails and periodically replacing the worst one, leading to something resembling \"Embarassingly Parallel Search\" with single assignments per worker.\n\n**SharedTreeWorker class comment:** None provided in the header.\n\n## Answers to Specific Questions\n\n**ProtoTrail:** Described as \"an intermediate datastructure that can be synced with the shared tree and the local Trail as appropriate.\" It stores objective lower bounds and literals that have been branched on and later proven implied by prior decisions.\n\n**SyncWithSharedTree:** No class-level comment exists; it's a private method mentioned only in implementation context.\n\n**ReplaceTree:** Documented as \"Assigns a path prefix that the worker should explore.\"\n\n**Work-stealing or cube-and-conquer:** Neither term appears in the provided content.\n\n**Papers cited:** Only \"Scalable Parallelization of Learning Solvers\" by Graeme Gange and Peter Stuckey is explicitly mentioned. No formal citations or URLs are provided."}]},"uuid":"8d077609-9a2c-441a-847e-d52bee7dfc59","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:01:41.147Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"966ba0b1-67fb-4b27-b18f-d5489c9d4d0e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8d077609-9a2c-441a-847e-d52bee7dfc59","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6d05a19c340d22c4","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_017o2vcM1PDdeu7MSR1Tosvr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have comprehensive information. Let me compile the research findings.\n\n---\n\n# OR-Tools CP-SAT shared_tree Workers 深度调研\n\n## 1. shared_tree 是什么\n\nshared_tree 是 CP-SAT 中一种**协作式 subsolver**，多个 worker 共享同一棵搜索树而不是各跑独立的 portfolio 实例。SharedTreeManager 维护一棵全局决策树，把不同子树（leaf 路径）分给不同 worker 探索，worker 之间通过 nogood 和 objective bound 交换避免重复探索。和 portfolio 的本质区别在 cpsat-primer 也强调过：portfolio \"不切分搜索空间\"，shared_tree 切分。源码注释直接说\"intended to investigate Graeme Gange & Peter Stuckey's proposal: Scalable Parallelization of Learning Solvers\"，也就是 LCG 学习型求解器的搜索树并行化。\n\n## 2. 关键参数（sat_parameters.proto）\n\n- `shared_tree_num_workers = 235 [default = -1]`：负值用启发式自动选；正值 = 完整 worker 线程数\n- `use_shared_tree_search = 236 [default = false]`：内部标志，**注释明说 \"Users should not set this directly\"**\n- `shared_tree_max_nodes_per_worker = 238 [default = 10000]`：树总节点上限/worker；超过后 worker 退化为 portfolio\n- `shared_tree_split_strategy = 239 [default = SPLIT_STRATEGY_AUTO]`：5 种枚举（AUTO≈DISCREPANCY、DISCREPANCY、OBJECTIVE_LB、BALANCED_TREE、FIRST_PROPOSAL）\n- `shared_tree_open_leaves_per_worker = 281 [default = 2.0]`：每 worker 平均维持多少未分配 leaf\n- `shared_tree_worker_min_restarts_per_subtree = 282 [default = 1]`：worker 替换\"差\"子树前要重启多少次（按平均 LBD 判断）\n- `shared_tree_worker_enable_trail_sharing = 295 [default = true]`：共享被树决策蕴含的 literal\n- `shared_tree_worker_enable_phase_sharing = 304 [default = true]`：归还子树时附带 target phase\n- `shared_tree_balance_tolerance = 305 [default = 1]`：树深\"够平衡\"的容忍度，只对 BALANCED_TREE/DISCREPANCY 生效\n- `shared_tree_split_min_dtime = 328 [default = 0.1]`：worker 提议 split 之间的最小 dtime\n- 注意：用户问的 `shared_tree_worker_objective_split_probability` 在最新 stable proto 找不到（已被替换/移除）\n\n`optimize_with_lb_tree_search = 188` 是**完全不同的东西**——它是单 worker 的 MIP 风格树搜索，专门用来抬 LB，不是共享树。\n\n## 3. 何时启用（关键启发式）\n\n`cp_model_solver_helpers.cc` 里默认启发式：\n```\nif (params->shared_tree_num_workers() == -1) {\n  if (有 objective)\n    num_shared_tree_workers = (num_workers - 16) / 2;\n  else\n    num_shared_tree_workers = (num_workers - 8) * 3 / 4;\n}\n```\n含义：**有目标函数的 (优化)，要 16 worker 以上才有 1 个 shared_tree；纯可行性问题，要 8 worker 以上才有 1 个**。8 worker 优化场景下默认是 0 个 shared_tree worker。\n\n## 4. 算法机制\n\n(a) Manager 在根插一个假决策建初始 leaf 池。(b) Worker 跑本地 SAT 时携带一个 ProtoTrail（路径前缀+蕴含 literal+objective lb）。(c) Worker 通过 `TrySplitTree()` 把当前 leaf 按 split_strategy 切两半，一份自己继续走、一份回到 manager 队列。(d) `ReplaceTree()` 把空 leaf 分给空闲或 LBD 表现差的 worker。(e) `CloseTree()` 关闭已证明无改进解的子树。(f) 同步靠 `SyncWithSharedTree`/`SyncWithLocalTrail`，互斥靠 `absl::Mutex mu_`。和 portfolio 区别：portfolio 只共享 clause 和 bound，搜索空间重叠；shared_tree **物理切分** leaf 到不同 worker。\n\n## 5. 学术参考\n\n主参考：Gange & Stuckey, \"Scalable Parallelization of Learning Solvers\"（pstuckey/papers/parallelCP.pdf）。后续工作 \"Parallelising Lazy Clause Generation with Trail Sharing\"（CP 2024+，Springer）正是 `shared_tree_worker_enable_trail_sharing` 的来源。**关联但不等同**于 SAT 圈的 Cube-and-Conquer（Heule 2011, lookahead 切 cube 给 CDCL）和 Mallob 的 distributed portfolio——CP-SAT 是同进程多线程的 work-reassignment（不是经典 work-stealing），更接近 \"Embarrassingly Parallel Search with reassignment\"（注释原话）。\n\n## 6. GitHub issues / 讨论\n\nissue #3662（Perron 团队修过）：4 worker 证不出 optimal、5 worker 秒证，原因正是 5 worker 才能激活某些 dual subsolver。Perron 在 i3TF_Szuz_k 讨论里给出经典口径：\"最佳性能 8 线程，要真正 speedup 必须有 8 物理核\"。9.12 release notes 明确：\"Improve shared tree workers, implement job affinity with workers\"——一个 85s→56s 的 8-worker benchmark 提升被点名。\n\n## 7. 对我们 placement 问题的预期效果\n\n我们硬候选大量 INFEASIBLE 证明：shared_tree **理论上对 INFEASIBILITY 友好**，因为论文原话 \"workers can prove infeasibility of subproblems independently\"，子树各自死路只需 close，不需要 global coordination（optimality 才需要）。但有两个坑：(1) 我们 ghost rectangle + binding 是高耦合约束，子树切分后两边各自带的 clause DB 可能水土不服，trail_sharing 才出现就是为这个；(2) 当前 8 worker，按默认启发式 shared_tree 数量 = 0（有 objective 时 (8-16)/2 = -4 → max(0,…) = 0），**目前我们根本没启用**。\n\n## 8. 同进程 / 跨进程\n\n同一 process 的 multi-thread，靠 `absl::Mutex` 同步，**不是** Mallob/distributed 那种多机 SAT。我们的 `exact_parallel_scheduler.py` 跨进程（multiprocessing）每个进程内还是只用 CP-SAT 单进程的 num_workers，shared_tree 在每个进程内独立运作。\n\n## 9. 调试和监控\n\nCP-SAT log 里 worker table 会出现名为 `shared_tree`（小写下划线）的行，统计 deterministic_time、conflicts、branches、restarts。\"Clauses shared\" 表里也会显示 shared_tree workers 共享的 clause 数。cpsat-logutils 可以解析这些。如果日志没出现 shared_tree 行，说明启发式没启用（worker 不够）。\n\n## 10. 2024-2026 进展\n\n9.10 引入 `enable_trail_sharing`（field 295）+ `enable_phase_sharing`（304）+ `balance_tolerance`（305）。9.11 引入 `split_min_dtime`（328）抑制过度切分争用。**9.12（2025/02）Release Notes 主线项：\"Improve shared tree workers, implement job affinity\"**。9.13 持续微调，没有破坏性改动。\n\n---\n\n## 我们项目的实战建议\n\n**当前状况**：8 worker + 优化目标，默认启发式给 0 个 shared_tree worker。意味着 Round 1-4 提到 shared_tree 时其实在我们配置下根本没跑。\n\n**建议实测路径**（按 PROJECT_LOCK.md，所有都进 deterministic 实验，不入 certified 前先观察）：\n\n1. **基线**：保持 `shared_tree_num_workers = -1` 但记录 log 验证 0；\n2. **手动启用**：扩到 `num_workers = 16`，让默认启发式自动给 (16-16)/2=0……还是 0，所以要**直接显式设** `shared_tree_num_workers = 2`（在 8 worker 下占 25%）或 `= 4`（占 50%）；\n3. **针对 INFEASIBLE 候选**：硬候选证伪是我们瓶颈，shared_tree 理论上加速 UNSAT 证明，重点跑这一类；split_strategy 试 `SPLIT_STRATEGY_OBJECTIVE_LB`（要求 lb 等于 global lb 才切），对纯 feasibility 等价于 FIRST_PROPOSAL；\n4. **可调旋钮**：`shared_tree_max_nodes_per_worker` 默认 10000 对 70x70 candidate placement 估计够；`open_leaves_per_worker` 从 2.0 试到 4.0 看是否减少 worker 空转；\n5. **观察日志**：subsolver table 里 shared_tree 那行的 conflicts/sec、closed 子树数；如果 shared_tree close 数远高于 portfolio worker，说明它在拉车；\n6. **风险**：trail_sharing 默认 true 但和我们 ghost rectangle 后处理 hint 可能冲突，先单独跑 `enable_trail_sharing=false` 做对照；\n7. **绝对不能**：把 shared_tree 结果当 certified proof 的一部分写进 checkpoint（违反 AI 安全契约的延伸——这条对所有\"实验性 subsolver\"都适用）。\n\nSources:\n- [or-tools/sat_parameters.proto (stable)](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto)\n- [or-tools/work_assignment.h (stable)](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/work_assignment.h)\n- [Issue #3662 — num_workers threshold](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3662)\n- [Issue #3590 — non-determinism](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3590)\n- [v9.12 Release Notes](https://github.com/google/or-tools/releases/tag/v9.12)\n- [CP-SAT Primer - Parameters](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html)\n- [CP-SAT Primer - Understanding the Log](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html)\n- [Gange & Stuckey - Parallelizing Constraint Programming with Learning](https://people.eng.unimelb.edu.au/pstuckey/papers/parallelCP.pdf)\n- [Parallelising LCG with Trail Sharing (Springer)](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-95973-8_13)\n- [Perron & Didier - The CP-SAT-LP Solver (CP 2023)](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol280-cp2023/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3.pdf)\n- [or-tools-discuss - Parallel search problem](https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/i3TF_Szuz_k)\n- [cpsat-logutils](https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-logutils)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2539,"cache_read_input_tokens":40763,"output_tokens":4149,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2539},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":4149,"cache_read_input_tokens":40763,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2539,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2539,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaotC2D7oUwTHwLJ6jcoH","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b74fd272-e5a6-419c-9ca8-19be810649f8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:02:52.231Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
